  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Declared exact portable CPU baselines and dependency dispatch for Linux x64/arm64, macOS arm64, and Windows x64. Builders derive GMP, OpenBLAS, FFLAS, M4RI, igraph, ff_poly, and smalljac policy from one fingerprinted authority and record byte-bound dependency receipts. The release CLI independently reconstructs each expected profile, validates exact source/interface/output/build authority, and reports receipt and output identities. Linux x64 OpenBLAS includes the SSE2 Opteron kernel as its x86-64-v1 floor; newer kernels remain runtime-dispatched. Rehashed hostile-receipt tests cover native flags, host cache detection, mismatched profiles, and incomplete/tampered outputs.",
    "risks": [
      "Clean dependency builds and binary inspection remain the platform release builders' responsibility; this lane validates builder declarations and synthetic complete receipts.",
      "The isolated worktree's broad portable tier cannot run native integration cases without built FLINT/FFLAS artifacts; focused policy tests, architecture checks, strict Python, and the runner manifest pass.",
      "This CPU profile is deliberately independent of the Linux glibc, libstdc++, and libatomic compatibility contract."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Land on the shared release baseline and consume the clean Linux x64, macOS arm64, and Windows x64 validation results.",
      "Invoke scripts/release-cpu-profile.cjs from each official native packager after dependencies are staged.",
      "Retain clean-machine old-CPU execution and binary instruction inspection as independent release gates."
    ]
  }
